<h1>Your <%= REDIRECT_DOMAIN %> API access token</h1>

<p>
  <%= @inviter %> set up API access to
  <%= REDIRECT_DOMAIN %> for <strong><%= @user.email %></strong>.
</p>

<ul>
  <li>Token: <%= @api_token.name %></li>
  <li>Access: <%= api_token_access_label(@api_token) %></li>
  <li>Valid for: <%= api_token_lifetime_label(@api_token.lifetime_days) %> after you collect it</li>
  <% if @api_token.note.present? %>
    <li>Note: <%= @api_token.note %></li>
  <% end %>
</ul>

<p><a href="<%= @claim_url %>">Get your API token</a></p>

<p>
  This link works once and expires on <%= api_token_time(@api_token.claim_expires_at) %>.
  The token is shown only once, so store it somewhere safe, such as a password manager.
</p>

<p>
  Send the token in the <code>Authorization</code> header of each request:<br>
  <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;your token&gt;</code><br>
  API base URL: <%= @api_base_url %>
</p>

<p>If you weren't expecting this email, you can ignore it.</p>
